  <acqinfo id="7c847bb165b0922362260416d7df500e">
    <head>Immediate Source of Acquisition</head>
<p>Ford Foundation archive was deposited at RAC in 2011. Ford Foundation records, correspondence, reports, program files, and officers' papers were transferred to, and accessioned by the RAC beginning in 2011. Accessions continue as necessary.</p><p>
The first set of Stephen P. Marks Office Files was transferred to the RAC in 2018 by the Ford Foundation and was ingested by the RAC as Accession 2018:034. A later set of material was transferred to the RAC in 2019 and ingested as Accession 2019:054.</p>  </acqinfo>
  <scopecontent id="253f894ba64e1ba9a2232e5ff5d547cc">
    <head>Scope and Contents</head>
<p>Collection holds the office files of Ford Foundation Program Officer Stephen P. Marks. The files were created during Marks' time in the Human Rights and Governance Program (HRG) at Ford where he was responsible for grant-making decisions related to international human rights.</p><p>
The collection consists of only two series. The first series contains the chronological files Marks maintained to organize his correspondence and other documents, and the second series contains Marks' subject files.
Common types of material found within the collection include correspondence, memoranda, drafts, notes, reports, newspaper clippings, schedules, agendas, and speech transcripts.</p><p>
The collection is comprised of more than one accession of material. The chronological files in Series 1 originated from the first set of material that was transferred to the Rockefeller Archive Center in 2018 (Accession 2018:034). A later set of material was transferred to the RAC in 2019 (Accession 2019:054). The subject files in Series 2 originate from this accession.</p>  </scopecontent>
